@lens(user, developer)
@display("Lenses")
lenses: concept {
  | A tree has more than one kind of reader, and the docs show each the part it needs. A
  | lens is one of these views. The site you're reading has three: `user`, task first and
  | without the rules that bind an implementation, at the site's root; `developer`, the
  | language by topic with every rule on one line; and `explore`, the whole tree. The
  | switcher in the top bar moves between them and keeps your place.
  |
  | Every lens is built from the same tree in the same run, so no view can say something
  | another contradicts. A tree chooses its lenses in its [docs block](#tools.docs.extending.docs_block), as
  | `docs { lenses = [user, developer, explore] }`, can declare its own with `lens`, and
  | marks a node or a run of prose `@lens(user)` to keep it to the lenses it names.
}
